{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When your brother sinks and sells.</b> This teaches that a person may not sell his field except under the pressure of poverty (cf. Sifra)." "<b>that is his holding.</b> And not all of it — it teaches proper conduct, that one should leave a field for oneself." "<b>and redeem what his brother sold.</b> And the buyer cannot hold it back."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:20.557154322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}